{
  "description": "Wallet-history walk truncation semantics for reconcilePaymentAttempts / reconcile_payments. A walk that ends before the wallet runs out of rows (page cap, pass deadline, or a wallet that ignores `offset` and repeats a page) is TRUNCATED: a hash such a walk did not see is unproven, never proven absent, so it must be OMITTED from the results instead of reported not_found \u2014 reporting not_found would let a caller close a paid attempt. Pages are built by expanding `filler_rows` into settled incoming rows whose payment_hash is 56 'f' characters followed by the 8-digit zero-padded value of page*10000+index; both harnesses use the same expansion. `unusable_rows` adds that many rows the wallet sent but no engine can normalize (payment_hash present and not 64 hex), after the page's own rows: a harness whose fake client returns raw pages appends such rows and lets the walk's normalizer drop them; a harness whose fake client returns normalized pages reports the count as the page's skipped-row count. Either way the page the WALLET sent was full, so it never proves the wallet ran out of rows. Physical offsets advance by the returned raw row count (including unusable rows); a short nonempty page is not exhaustion. Harnesses map each descriptor to its cumulative physical offset, not floor(offset/20). Missing descriptors represent an actual empty page.",
  "page_limit": 20,
